\begin_layout Chapter
Familiarity based Genetic Programming
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
In the following, the implementation of the approach to link genetic programming
 with familiarity is presented and justified.
 As a reference for familiarity, a heuristic developed by an expert to solve
 a problem (origin) is used.
 As a measure for the changes some factors are presented that have led to
 the use of the Tree Edit Distance (TED), which calculates the number of
 differences of computational trees.
 The fitness of the candidates is calculated as a possible path via a regression
, whose data is generated by black box approaches.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
For the implementation a GP framework was developed, which implements pareto
 genetic programming, is strongly typed and uses tensorflow for evaluation.
 Furthermore, the use of fixed nodes was introduced as an optional anchor
 to expert heuristics.
\end_layout

