\begin_inset Formula 
\[
d_{bounded}\begin{cases}
0 & d(\min(\max(x_{ik},a_{\min}),a_{\max}),x_{jk})=0\\
\min(d,\text{penalty}) & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
\]

\end_inset

The aim is to find a mathematical formula that produces moderate results
 and does not produce overfitted extreme values even in special cases.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

Here, a second measure, which aims to produce moderate values, was mixed
 with the main measure, which should indicate the distance to the target
 solution.
 The second measure automatically becomes the KO criterion for candidates,
 single wrong points distort the regression error beyond recognition.
 This slowed down the training process extremely, furthermore, the most
 effective solution was not a formula that only generates moderate values,
 but the use of the min and max function.
 [xxx]
