\begin_layout Subsection
Black box: Sarsa with Tiling
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
As a black box solution, the leader of the gym-leaderboards was chosen,
 which uses a SARSA approach with tiling and thus reaches the goal of a
 maximum of 110 steps after 75 training episodes.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset citation
LatexCommand cite
key "xiao2019"
literal "true"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Foot
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
The gym-environment has a leaderboard containing the approaches that have
 been able to learn the fastest to create a policy that solves the problem
 in steps of less than 
\begin_inset Formula $110$
\end_inset

.
 
\begin_inset CommandInset href
LatexCommand href
name "https://github.com/openai/gym/wiki/Leaderboard"
target "https://github.com/openai/gym/wiki/Leaderboard"
literal "false"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset

 The average reward of the SARSA-agent is, with an average reward of 
\begin_inset Formula $-103$
\end_inset

, outperforming the simple approach of a developer that will be introduced
 in 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "par:simple,-maximum-momentum"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"

\end_inset

